    <DataNode elementId="CPD-7323" textLabel="methanophenazine" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="VRHMBACMYZITGD-QAAQOENVSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="500" centerY="400" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, zhang">Several unusual cofactors are involved in methanogenesis. One of those is |FRAME: CPD-7323|, a 2-hydroxyphenazine derivative which is linked via an ether bridge to a pentaisoprenoid side chain |CITS: [10941105]|. The reduced form of |FRAME: CPD-7323 Methanophenazine| serves as the electron donor for |FRAME: EC-1.8.98.1|.</Comment>
